      "body": "Stack from [ghstack](https://github.com/ezyang/ghstack/tree/0.12.0) (oldest at bottom):\n* __->__ #5368\n\n#4772 exported its A10G goldens on a base that predated #5250 (in-place\nbf16 Linear WGRAD accumulation), which itself re-baselined every A10G\ngolden. The final ghstack rebase onto #5250 kept #4772's stale values, so\nthe committed real_pg goldens never matched the landed code: step-1\ngrad_norm already differs (the WGRAD accumulation change), and the\ndivergence grows from step 2. The PR's real-PG CI only ran the required\nsubset, which excludes these tests; its fake-PG job failed on both.\n\nThese tests intentionally verify the new batch-wise aux-loss policy (the\nexpert-bias policy is kept only for gpt_oss_pp via\n_use_expert_bias_load_balancing), so this refreshes values without\nchanging configs.\n\nProvenance (torch 2.16.0.dev20261011+cu132, A10G, seed checkpoint per the\ntest definitions):\n- real_pg: bit-identical across two independent main runs -- job\n  114675094754 at 8b4a1300e and job 115529499679 at 50474ad60.\n- fake_pg: bit-identical across four independent ciflow/fake-pg runs on\n  PRs based on post-#4772 main (runs 38459347990, 38460226133,\n  38460414111, 38466591432) that do not touch core model code.",
